From: Oscar <osm1019@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 11:14:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] dodge: Clamp 8K video to 30fps to fix freeze after using
 4K120

Enabling real-time 1080p/4K 120fps adds 120 to the rear_main video fps
allow-list in camera_unit_feature_config.protobuf. That list is per-camera
and has no per-resolution scoping, so once 120fps is selected at 4K the
app's fps state stays 120 when switching to 8K. The UI correctly hides the
120 option and shows "8K-30", but nothing rewrites the stored value.

MediaRecorder is then configured for 7680x4320@120 and the video core
rejects it:

  msm_vidc_check_core_mbps: Hardware overloaded. needed 15552000, max 7833600

8K is 129600 macroblocks/frame, so the core budget caps it near 60fps and
120 is roughly 2x over. prepare() fails and the app retries ~23 times over
~5.5s - that burst is the preview freeze when switching modes, and 8K
recording fails outright.

Clamp to 30fps at the three points that actually configure the recorder
(obfuscated names from this build):

  u0.A(II)                 setVideoSize runs after setVideoFrameRate, so
                           re-apply 30fps once the 8K width is known; this
                           is the path the mode switch takes
  u0.v(CamcorderProfile)   clamp profile.videoFrameRate on entry, which
                           covers the setProfile branch used when recording
  g.buildSession           send video_30fps for the session at
                           video_size_8k (FPSPresenter)

1080p120 and 4K120 are untouched - they never reach these branches, and the
real-time 120fps rate override is left intact. Verified on device: switching
4K120 -> 8K now logs zero encoder failures (was 23) with no preview stall,
and 8K30 records.

This patch is the only one required on older OxygenOS releases; the 7.5fps
and 720p issues appear with OxygenOS 16.0.8.301 and are covered by the
following patches.
---
 smali_classes12/ak/u0.smali | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 smali_classes28/ja/g.smali  | 15 +++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 39 insertions(+)

